text:
marie: quick design review — I'm trying two options for the console on narrow screens: compact list (one-line rows, horizontal scroll) vs. stacked scroll (taller cards). also thinking about when the left nav should auto-collapse. screenshots in figma: https://figma.com/file/abcd1234 | pls react w/ thoughts :eyes:

alex: overall i prefer compact list for the activity table — keeps info density. main concern is truncation of long job names. maybe 2-line wrap max? :thinking_face:

marie: good call. 2-line wrap max sounds reasonable. how do people feel about auto-collapse breakpoint for the sidebar? current proposal is collapse < 920px then overlay at < 600px.

devin: 920px feels high — a lot of tablets would collapse. i'd do collapse at 768px, overlay at 480px. those map to common device widths.

marie: @devin can you sketch the CSS media points?

devin: sure — rough:
```
/* desktop */
@media (min-width: 769px) { .sidebar { expanded: true } }
/* tablet */
@media (max-width: 768px) and (min-width: 481px) { .sidebar { collapsed: true } }
/* mobile */
@media (max-width: 480px) { .sidebar { overlay: true } }
```

marie: thanks. that aligns with product's earlier notes.

sophia: accessibility nits: when sidebar collapses it must still be reachable via keyboard (focus trap?), and the toggle needs aria-expanded + aria-controls. touch targets should be >=44px. also ensure table row focus state is visible when rows are one-line.

jamal: perf note — horizontal scrolling tables force us to keep all columns rendered for virtualization to work cleanly. if we do one-line compact list with horizontal scroll we might need an inner scroll container and careful virtualization. could add a small cache to avoid jank.

alex: for long names truncation: show full on hover + accessible tooltip for keyboard users. also add a trailing ellipsis and a copy action in the row menu.

marie: copy tweak: instead of "Collapse sidebar" button label, use "Hide navigation" on mobile to be clearer. shorter text helps with small widths. thoughts?

sophia: "Hide navigation" reads better for screen readers. add visually-hidden text that announces "opens navigation" when toggled.

devin: mini UX question — with compact rows should we reduce vertical padding to 8px so density matches desktop? that'd help keep visible rows high.

alex: yes 8px feels fine but keep minimum touch area for interactive elements. shrink non-interactive spacing first.

ui-bot: uploaded image preview: https://assets.company.com/previews/compact-list-v2.png :sparkles:

marie: ok action items:
- dev: implement breakpoints (768 / 480) and share a branch
- ux: finalize wording for toggle -> "Hide navigation" and add aria changes
- eng: validate virtualization perf for horizontal scroll
- design: lock down 2-line max and 8px row padding
I'll open a PR template and link comps. thanks all :raised_hands:

alex: cool, i'll try gestures on an iPad later and report back.
